# Lesson numbering (sprints)

Apply when authoring or renaming co-authored **lessons** under `docs/notes/sprints/`.

Full co-authoring flow: [`coauthoring_protocol.mdc`](coauthoring_protocol.mdc). Sprint records: [`docs/notes/sprint-record-template.md`](../docs/notes/sprint-record-template.md).

## Rules (Sprint 168 onward)

1. **Per-sprint restart** — Lesson numbers start at **1** for each new Jira sprint. Do **not** continue a global counter across sprints (e.g. do not carry Sprint 167’s Lesson 22 into Sprint 168 as Lesson 23).
2. **Workstream directory = one parent lesson** — A curriculum folder such as `sprint-{NNN}/ga-adapter-wiring/` is **one** numbered lesson (e.g. Lesson **2**). Sub-lessons inside that folder use **ascending lowercase letters**: **2a**, **2b**, **2c**, …
3. **Filenames** — Prefer `lesson-{N}{letter?}-{short-slug}.md` (e.g. `lesson-2a-state-configs-ga.md`). An optional overview may live at the sprint root or as `lesson-{N}-{workstream-slug}.md` next to the folder.
4. **Handoff labels** — Match the ID: **“Lesson 2a ready”**, not a parallel global number.
5. **Disambiguation in cross-sprint prose** — When linking across sprints, qualify the sprint: “Sprint 168 Lesson 1a” vs “Sprint 167 Lesson 20a”.

## Do not renumber

- **Sprints before 168** — Leave historical lesson IDs (e.g. Sprint 165 Lesson 09, Sprint 166 Lesson 14b, Sprint 167 Lesson 20a) as shipped. New work in those folders may keep the old scheme if extending an existing series; prefer the rules above only for **new** sprint folders from 168 on.
- Do not mass-rewrite `CHANGELOG.md` / `DECISIONS.md` history solely to renumber; update **living** sprint curriculum and records.

## Examples

| Layout | IDs |
|--------|-----|
| `sprint-168/lesson-1-ga-transform-and-load.md` + `ga-transform-and-load/lesson-1a-…` … `lesson-1g-…` | Lesson **1** overview; sub-lessons **1a–1g** |
| `sprint-168/ga-adapter-wiring/lesson-2a-…` … `lesson-2f-…` | Workstream Lesson **2**; packages **2a–2f** |
| Next sprint | Starts again at Lesson **1** (new workstream folders get **1a…**, **2a…**, …) |

### Sprint 168 remapping (2026-07-31)

| Former (global-style) | Current (sprint-local) |
|----------------------|-------------------------|
| 23 / 23a–23e / 24 / 25 | **1** / **1a–1e** / **1f** / **1g** |
| 26–31 (`ga-adapter-wiring`, first cut) | **2a–2f** then **2a** leaf inserted → **2a–2g** (2026-07-31) |

## Agent checklist

When adding a lesson package:

- [ ] Confirm the **current sprint** number
- [ ] Assign the next free **sprint-local** parent number (or next letter in an existing workstream folder)
- [ ] Do not invent a number higher than prior sprints’ last lesson “to stay unique”
- [ ] Update the workstream `README.md` index and sprint record task tracker to the new ID
